SUMMARY:Relax and Rejuvenate: Sound Bath and Meditation
DESCRIPTION:Sound Bath Experience  Allow yourself to surrender to the hea
 ling power of sound\, creating space for peace\, renewal\, and deep inner
  harmony. This offering begins with a brief guided meditation\, followed 
 by an extended Sound Bath featuring the resonant tones of crystal bowls a
 nd other healing instruments. The soothing frequencies help promote deep 
 relaxation\, renewal\, and overall physical and emotional well-being.What
  to Expect:Introduction and Intention Setting – A short meditation to c
 enter the mind and prepare for the journey.  Sound Bath – Experience th
 e immersive power of sound as vibrations wash over you\, supporting deep 
 rest and energetic balance.  Closing and Integration – Time for reflect
 ion\, gentle reawakening\, and optional sharing.  What to Bring:  To enha
 nce your comfort\, we recommend bringing:A yoga mat\, blanket\, pillow\, 
 and eye mask—whatever supports you in fully relaxing while lying down f
 or an hour.  A small personal item for the altar to honor someone or some
 thing\, set an intention\, or infuse with positive energy.  Seats are lim
 ited! We have room for 15 faculty/staff participants for this event. We w
 ill enable a waitlist if we reach that cap.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p style="font-weight: 400\;"><strong>Sound 
 Bath Experience</strong></p><p style="font-weight: 400\;">  Allow yoursel
 f to surrender to the healing power of sound\, creating space for peace\,
  renewal\, and deep inner harmony. This offering begins with a brief guid
 ed meditation\, followed by an extended Sound Bath featuring the resonant
  tones of crystal bowls and other healing instruments. The soothing frequ
 encies help promote deep relaxation\, renewal\, and overall physical and 
 emotional well-being.</p><p><strong>What to Expect:</strong></p><ul><li><
 strong>Introduction and Intention Setting</strong> – A short meditation
  to center the mind and prepare for the journey.  </li><li><strong>Sound 
 Bath</strong> – Experience the immersive power of sound as vibrations w
 ash over you\, supporting deep rest and energetic balance.  </li><li><str
 ong>Closing and Integration</strong> – Time for reflection\, gentle rea
 wakening\, and optional sharing.  </li></ul><p><strong>What to Bring:</st
 rong></p><p>  To enhance your comfort\, we recommend bringing:</p><ul><li
 >A yoga mat\, blanket\, pillow\, and eye mask—whatever supports you in 
 fully relaxing while lying down for an hour.  </li><li>A small personal i
 tem for the altar to honor someone or something\, set an intention\, or i
 nfuse with positive energy.  </li></ul><p><em><strong>Seats are limited! 
 We have room for 15 faculty/staff participants for this event. We will en
 able a waitlist if we reach that cap.</strong></em></p>
