 Q0pQJegQICxAB)\, The Hot Corner (https://www.portlandpicklesbaseball.com/
 seating-chart)  &#160\;4727 SE 92nd Avenue&#160\;  Portland\, OR 97266  C
 heck in starts at 5:30 p.m.  Stadium opens at 5:45 p.m.  First pitch is a
 t 7:05 p.m.  Tickets - $30/person  Sponsored by the Class of 2021\, and t
 heir classmate\, Pickles GM Courtney Schmidt (https://www.portlandpickles
 baseball.com/news/courtney-schmidt-promoted-to-general-manager-of-the-por
 tland-pickles)\, alumni will enjoy watching the game at Walker Stadium fr
 om the private\, covered venue the "Hot Corner" along the third base line
 . Show your L&amp\;C spirit in orange and black while enjoying that eveni
 ng's theme "Spooky Scary Haunted Night".&#160\;Purchase your tickets toda
 y (https://engage.lclark.edu/register/?id=305437e0-2ea5-4e1a-9319-3ebfd4f
 8e661)  Do you have questions about this event?  Take a look below and if
  you don't find an answer\, email Amanda Valley (avalley@lclark.edu (mail
 to:avalley@lclark.edu)) for more information.  How do I get my ticket for
  game day?Instead of physical tickets\, your name will be on a list to ga
 in entry into the "Hot Corner".  Staff will be available at Walker Stadiu
 m starting at 5:30 p.m. to assist you with checking in and finding your s
 eats.  Access to the "Hot Corner" is ADA compliant.&#160\;  Seating in th
 e "Hot Corner" is not assigned and will be first come\, first seated.    
 How do I get to Walker Stadium?Walker Stadium is located in Southeast Por
 tland within Lents Park. 4727 SE 92nd Ave\, Portland\, OR 97266  You can 
 find the location on Google Maps by following this link (https://www.goog
 le.com/maps?entry=mc&amp\;output=search&amp\;q=walker%20stadium&amp\;sa=X
 &amp\;sca_esv=579237292&amp\;source=lnms&amp\;sqi=2&amp\;ved=2ahUKEwji3sv
 I5aiCAxVhD0QIHfugBjEQ0pQJegQICxAB).&#160\;  Tri Met's #17 bus easily acce
 sses Lents Park and using a rideshare (Lyft or Uber) is also encouraged. 
  Coming from the 2011 Pre-Pickles Social at The Zed? Here is a map with w
 alking directions to Walker Stadium (https://www.lclark.edu/live/files/38
 036-2011-social-at-the-zed-to-walker-stadium).    Where do I park?Walker 
 Stadium has limited parking spaces in lots located around Lents Park. Mos
 t parking options are on-street\, predominately along SE 92nd Avenue. See
  the map (https://www.google.com/maps/place/Walker+Stadium+-+Portland+Pic
 kles+Baseball/@45.488401\,-122.5716889\,17.25z/data=!4m6!3m5!1s0x5495a02f
 e2904ecb:0xfb951684341a7986!8m2!3d45.488337!4d-122.5695783!16s%2Fg%2F11cp
 7g_fly?entry=ttu&amp\;g_ep=EgoyMDI2MDUwMi4wIKXMDSoASAFQAw%3D%3D) for deta
 ils on lot locations.  ADA parking is available in Lents Park lots. Arriv
 ing before 5:45 p.m. is recommended to secure one of these spaces.    Can
  I purchase additional tickets for other classmates\, friends\, or family
  members?We expect this event to sell out\, but tickets are available for
  purchase through the Alumni Weekend registration (https://engage.lclark.
 edu/register/?id=305437e0-2ea5-4e1a-9319-3ebfd4f8e661).  Online purchasin
 g ends on June 4\, 2026 at 11:59 p.m. and cost $30 per person.  Tickets p
 urchased after June 4\, 2026 are $35 per person. Please email avalley@lcl
 ark.edu (mailto:avalley@lclark.edu) to check on availability.  Walk-in pu
 rchasing may be available but is not guaranteed. Email avalley@lclark.edu
  (mailto:avalley@lclark.edu) or call 503-768-7941 to check availability.
