DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20260618T170000
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Trauma-Informed Breathwork for Nervous System Regulation in Clini
 cal Practice (Online)
DESCRIPTION:This experiential workshop introduces clinicians to trauma-in
 formed breathwork as a practical\, ethical\, and accessible tool for nerv
 ous system regulation in clinical settings.  Grounded in somatic psycholo
 gy\, polyvagal-informed approaches\, and breath-based interventions\, thi
 s training provides clinicians with concrete techniques they can immediat
 ely integrate into their work with clients experiencing anxiety\, trauma-
 related stress\, and nervous system dysregulation.  The workshop is organ
 ized around a four-phase somatic arc—Root\, Release\, Integrate\, and E
 mbody—which offers clinicians a structured framework for understanding 
 how breathwork and somatic interventions can be applied at different stag
 es of trauma recovery.  Participants will learn how to use breathwork for
  stabilization and resourcing\, how to safely support emotional and somat
 ic release\, and how to facilitate integration through gentle parts-based
  and inner child–informed practices.  In clinical settings\, this train
 ing emphasizes integration before embodiment\, ensuring safety\, pacing\,
  and nervous system stabilization. This sequencing helps clinicians devel
 op a clear understanding of when and how to use breath-based intervention
 s in an ethical\, trauma-informed\, culturally responsive\, and clinicall
 y sound manner.Following this workshop\, participants will be able to:Des
 cribe how trauma impacts the nervous system and breathing patterns.  Expl
 ain the four phases of somatic trauma recovery: Root\, Release\, Integrat
 e\, and Embody.  Demonstrate at least three trauma-informed breathwork te
 chniques for nervous system regulation.Identify appropriate breath-based 
 interventions based on a client's window of tolerance and readiness.  Int
 egrate breathwork and somatic awareness into existing clinical models.  D
 etails &amp\; RegistrationDate: Thursday\, June 18\, 2026\, 1-5 p.m. PT\,
  OnlineInstructor: Caroline McGrath\, LPC\, NCCDetails: $105\, includes 4
  CEUs. Alumni and Adjuncts save 20%.&#160\;  This workshop is currently f
 ull. Add your name to the waitlist. (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735424/
 ?epid=a1aUY000002ULDx)  GSEC Clinical Mental Health Supervisors\, Faculty
 \, and Staff\, please email cce@lclark.edu (mailto:cce@lclark.edu) to be 
 added to the waitlist.Accessibility: We are committed to making our event
 s accessible to all needs and abilities. When registering\, please let us
  know your access needs. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or cce@lclark.edu (ma
 ilto:cce@lclark.edu)&#160\;with questions.Please note: Discounted &#x2018
 \;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for current students only and d
 o not include continuing education credit (CEU/PDUs)About the InstructorC
 aroline McGrath\, LPC\, NCC is a Licensed Professional Counselor\, Certif
 ied Trauma-Informed Breathwork and HypnoBreathwork Facilitator\, Certifie
 d Somatic Jungian Coach\, and Certified TRE® Provider. She is the founde
 r of Soul of the Lotus®\, a practice devoted to somatic healing\, depth 
 psychology\, and embodied transformation.  Caroline's work integrates cli
 nical counseling\, nervous system regulation\, breathwork\, and inner chi
 ld–informed approaches to support deep\, lasting change. She works with
  college students\, young adults\, and midlife women navigating anxiety\,
  identity shifts\, and life transitions.  In addition to her clinical pra
 ctice\, she leads professional trainings for therapists and helping profe
 ssionals\, as well as retreats and transformational programs for midlife 
 women. Her teaching emphasizes experiential learning\, trauma-informed pr
 actice\, and practical somatic tools that clinicians can confidently inte
 grate into their work.New workshops and trainings are added to our calend
 ar regularly. For the latest on professional development related to your 
 specific interests\, sign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.tfafor
 ms.net/4735441)
