 /strong> Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for 
 current students only and <strong>do not</strong> include continuing educ
 ation credit (CEU/PDUs)</em></p></div></li></ul></div><hr /><h2><strong>A
 bout the Instructors</strong></h2><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>L
 eslie Rodgers</strong> is a licensed clinical social worker and registere
 d ASIST (Applied Suicide Intervention Skills) trainer with over 20 years 
 experience working with children and adults in various therapeutic settin
 gs\, including group homes\, psychiatric hospitals\, and schools. Her cur
 rent work has involved implementing best practice procedures and providin
 g staff development in student threat assessment\, suicide prevention\, a
 nd crisis response for school districts. She holds a BA from the Universi
 ty of Texas and a Masters in Social Work from Portland State University.<
 /p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong>Kathy Wilson-Fey</strong> is a r
 egistered ASIST Trainer and has clinical therapy and teaching experience 
 in a variety of settings\, including community college\, community mental
  health\, and an international university. She has 15 years of experience
  as a mental health specialist in public schools\, where she worked with 
 students and families\, trained school staff on suicide intervention\, an
 d coordinated school support during crises. Kathy is fluent in Spanish an
 d is committed to equity work and cultural competence. She holds a BA fro
 m Whitman College and a Masters in Counseling Psychology from the Univers
 ity of Oregon.</p><div id="lw_widget_470b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget
