 k College\, Valentina provides psychotherapy\, teaches\, and develops pro
 grams to support diverse and underserved populations\, including Ukrainia
 n students. She is also the Co-Founder and Vice President of DAWN Inc.\, 
 where she leads humanitarian and medical aid initiatives in Ukraine and s
 upports refugee integration locally.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  V
 alentina has presented at several conferences\, including the Northwest R
 egional Equity Conference\, on the needs of Ukrainians and the importance
  of culturally responsive\, trauma-informed care. She has also spoken to 
 policymakers\, healthcare providers\, and community leaders about the ong
 oing challenges faced by Ukrainians and ways to strengthen systems of sup
 port both locally and abroad.<br />  Through her clinical\, educational\,
  and nonprofit work\, Valentina is recognized for advancing resilience\, 
 equity\, and culturally informed trauma care in both local and internatio
 nal contexts.</p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;"><strong><picture class="lw
 _image lw_image112607  lw_align_right"><source type="image/webp" srcset="
 https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/91/width/200/height/200/11
 2607_Yulia_by_Miri_square.webp 2x\, https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/sca
 le/3x/gid/91/width/200/height/200/112607_Yulia_by_Miri_square.webp 3x" da
 ta-origin="responsive"/><source type="image/jpeg" srcset="https://www.lcl
 ark.edu/live/image/scale/2x/gid/91/width/200/height/200/112607_Yulia_by_M
 iri_square.rev.1774974310.jpg 2x\, https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/scal
 e/3x/gid/91/width/200/height/200/112607_Yulia_by_Miri_square.rev.17749743
 10.jpg 3x" data-origin="responsive"/><img width="200" height="200" alt=""
  data-alt="" data-decoration="true" src="https://www.lclark.edu/live/imag
 e/gid/91/width/200/height/200/112607_Yulia_by_Miri_square.rev.1774974310.
 jpg" title="Yulia by Miri square" srcset="https://www.lclark.edu/live/ima
 ge/scale/2x/gid/91/width/200/height/200/112607_Yulia_by_Miri_square.rev.1
 774974310.jpg 2x\, https://www.lclark.edu/live/image/scale/3x/gid/91/widt
 h/200/height/200/112607_Yulia_by_Miri_square.rev.1774974310.jpg 3x" data-
 max-w="2974" data-max-h="2975" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></pi
 cture>Yulia Brockdorf\, RD\, LD\, CDCES\, CST\, NCC\, LPC\, BC-ADM\, BC-T
 MH\, LMHC\, FAIHM\, LN\, CD\, ACS\, FAWM</strong>&#160\;is a Ukrainian-Am
 erican trauma psychotherapist and registered dietitian specializing in tr
 eating complex trauma and culturally competent care. She is the developer
  of the first combat psychotherapy model designed for delivery in active 
 combat zones and has co-authored peer-reviewed publications on the psycho
 logical impact of drone warfare. Ms. Brockdorf provides direct psychother
 apy to Ukrainian defenders along Ukraine's front lines and has trained me
 ntal health professionals\, psychiatry residents\, and healthcare provide
 rs on trauma-informed approaches and working with Ukrainian populations.<
 /p><p style="line-height: 1.5\;">  Ms. Brockdorf developed the trauma and
  mental health course module <em>Connecting with Ukrainian Refugees: Meet
 ing Their Needs with Better Care and Key Service</em> for the Washington 
 State Department of Health and has lectured at universities and medical s
 chools on culturally responsive care for displaced populations. Her work 
 has been published in peer-reviewed literature and she has been featured 
 on Oregon's Think Out Loud and other media outlets. She previously served
  as Board President of the Oregon Board of Licensed Dietitians.</p><p sty
 le="line-height: 1.5\;">  As president and co-founder of DAWN\, Inc.\, Ms
 . Brockdorf has coordinated over $20 million in medical aid deliveries to
  Ukraine. She serves on the executive team of DefenseTech for Ukraine and
  advocates for U.S. support of Ukraine at state and federal levels\, incl
 uding meetings with NATO officials\, representatives of the European Parl
 iament\, and members of the Government of Ukraine\, and champions both lo
 cal and international efforts in global security.</p><div id="lw_widget_4
 70b39ba" class="lw_widget lw_widget_type_blurbs lw_widget_blurbs lw_widge
