DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260822
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260823
LOCATION:Hybrid
SUMMARY:Shift to Belonging: Sustainable & Critical Social Sciences Pedago
 gy in Challenging Times (Hybrid)
DESCRIPTION:Social Sciences teachers continue to experience increasing po
 litical and cultural pressure to reject the inclusion of culturally-respo
 nsive and critical curriculum in their pedagogy and classroom teaching. T
 his reality is made even more difficult by the isolation educators often 
 feel when they are not given space to reflect\, collaborate\, and create 
 with one another.  This creative curriculum course is designed for Oregon
  Social Sciences teachers who want to refresh their critical and reflecti
 ve practices and engage in conversation with fellow educators about how t
 o integrate anti-fascism and pro-imagination foundations into their pedag
 ogy and practice.  Participants in this class will:      Engage in facili
 tated conversations about the current political and cultural climate's im
 pact on inclusion\, belonging\, and critical practices in the classroom  
         Explore strategies around creating and integrating critical curri
 culum and reflecting on its power to impact student learning and agency  
         Evaluate how the new Oregon Social Science disciplinary practices
  and strategies can empower and sustain a critical pedagogy and increase 
 student engagement          Identify ways that intersectional and trauma-
 informed frameworks can build a climate of care and community in their So
 cial Science classroom          Design curriculum that challenges student
  thinking\, builds inquiry\, and allows for rigor and differentiation in 
 diverse classrooms—creating lessons and units for the coming year      
 Join with colleagues in community to refresh your strategies\, thinking\,
  and energy before returning for the fall semester.Course DetailsDates: I
 n-person Saturdays\, August 22 and October 10\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-4 p.m.\, at
  Lewis &amp\; Clark Graduate School\, with three hours of asynchronous wo
 rk to be completed online between meeting datesInstructor: Cari Zall\, MA
 TRegistration Options  Participants enrolled for continuing education cre
 dit will complete coursework in addition to the class meetings and asynch
 ronous reflection time in between. Those enrolled for PDUs will attend bo
 th class meetings and complete the asynchronous reflection time.&#160\;CE
  Credit: 1 semester hour of Graduate-level Continuing Education credit\, 
 $385Register for CE Credit (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735371)PDUs: $28
 5\, 15 PDUs. Alumni\, Adjuncts\, and Teacher Education Mentors and Superv
 isors save 20%.Register for PDUs (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/wf1W4MQ?epi
 d=a1aUY000002Zzib)Accessibility: We are committed to making our events ac
 cessible to all needs and abilities. When registering\, please let us kno
 w your access needs. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or cce@lclark.edu (mailto
 :cce@lclark.edu) with questions.About the Instructor Cari Zall (she/her) 
 is Clinical Assistant Professor and Social Studies Content Area Coordinat
 or &amp\; Advisor in the Secondary MAT Program at Lewis &amp\; Clark Grad
 uate School of Education and Counseling. She is also Director of Lewis &a
 mp\; Clark's Trans Youth Support and Advocacy Certificate Program (http:/
 /graduate%20student%20registrations%20are%20currently%20full.%20add%20you
 r%20name%20to%20the%20waitlist%20to%20be%20notified%20if%20space%20become
 s%20available/) and the College of Arts &amp\; Sciences Education Minor. 
 Cari brings to her equity education practice over 25 years of legal and e
 ducation experience. She has been a secondary and post-secondary educator
  for over 20 years\, with a concentration in Social Sciences\, Political 
 Science\, Civics\, and Teacher Education. She has been a curriculum desig
 ner and faculty administrator for a national online high school dropout r
 ecovery program and has designed and led Social Studies professional deve
 lopment in Oregon for over 15 years. She has experience in advocacy\, pro
 viding professional development\, and conflict resolution/mediation work.
 New workshops and trainings are added to our calendar regularly. For the 
 latest on professional development related to your specific interests\, s
 ign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.tfaforms.net/4735441)
