 1199" loading="lazy" data-optimized="true"/></picture> Matsya Siosal</str
 ong> has developed her skills in leadership and facilitation for over 25 
 years\, including roles with small and large for-profit corporations\, mi
 ssion-driven consumer goods companies\, higher education\, and as a consu
 ltant and entrepreneur. She has served as the director of the Center for 
 Community Engagement at Lewis &amp\; Clark since 2015\, after joining the
  department in 2010 to work in marketing and program management. Matsya i
 s also co-founder and managing partner of <a href="http://www.seaosalt.co
 m/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-saferedirecturl="https://www.goog
 le.com/url?q=http://www.seaosalt.com&amp\;source=gmail&amp\;ust=175338304
 4078000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw1p78DjRJB9GSrWHhA6LGkP">Sea-O-Salt Bath Company</a
 >. Matsya is an experienced certified facilitator of Courage &amp\; Renew
 al programs. She has facilitated Circle of Trust\, Courage to Lead\, and 
 Leading Together workshops and retreats since 2019\, and is trained as a 
 <a href="https://soulcollage.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-sa
 feredirecturl="https://www.google.com/url?q=https://soulcollage.com/&amp\
 ;source=gmail&amp\;ust=1753383044078000&amp\;usg=AOvVaw0R2GoVMeEDJcNYabHL
 8_ee">SoulCollage®</a> facilitator. As a facilitator and coach\, Matsya 
 supports mission-driven leaders in accessing their authentic voice\, and 
 finding clarity and self-trust so they can show up with wholeheartedness 
 and sustainability in their lives and work.</p><div id="lw_widget_470b39b
