DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261024
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261025
LOCATION:Online
SUMMARY:Reconnecting with Voice and Purpose: A Full-Day Workshop for Educ
 ators (Online)
DESCRIPTION:As busy educators\, it can be difficult to stay attuned to ou
 r own voice amid the many demands and pressures of our work. This Circle 
 of Trust (https://couragerenewal.org/about-us/)® workshop\, grounded in 
 the writing of Parker J. Palmer and the Center for Courage &amp\; Renewal
 \, offers a space for caring and committed educators to slow down\, refle
 ct\, and listen deeply to themselves and one another. Together\, we will 
 reconnect with the meaning and purpose that nourish our lives as educator
 s.  During this full-day\, online workshop we will have the opportunity t
 o reflect in solitude and in community with other educators to:      Shar
 e stories of our life and work experiences          Remember the hopes an
 d dreams that brought us to our vocation&#160\;          Entertain possib
 ilities for the year ahead      We will turn to our own stories and exper
 iences\, those of others in the circle\, as well as insights from diverse
  creators of poetry\, art\, music\, and other visual media to help us con
 nect with ourselves and one another. Join us as we courageously navigate 
 the realities of education in these challenging times.Details &amp\; Regi
 strationDate and Time: Saturday\, October 24\, 2026\, 9 a.m.-4 p.m. PT\, 
 OnlineFacilitators: Dawn Montgomery\, EdD\; and Liza Finkel\, PhDRegistra
 tion: $135\, Includes 6 PDUs. Alumni save 20%Register Online (https://lcl
 ark.tfaforms.net/4735427?epid=a1aUY000002iQld)Scholarship Fund:We strive 
 to keep our Courage retreats accessible to all who wish to participate. P
 lease consider making atax-deductible donation (https://engage.lclark.edu
 /register/gsecgiving?sys:gift:fund=4dfb9f4e-7351-4d84-91fe-531631c248c7&a
 mp\;sys:gift:notes=Courage%20and%20Renewal%20Retreats%20Scholarship%20Fun
 d)to our scholarship fund.Accessibility: We are committed to making our e
 vents accessible to all needs and abilities. When registering\, please le
 t us know your access needs. Contact us at 503-768-6040 or cce@lclark.edu
  (mailto:cce@lclark.edu)&#160\;with questions.Please note: Discounted &#x
 2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are for current students only a
 nd do not include continuing education credit (CEU/PDUs)About the Facilit
 atorsLiza Finkel\, PhD is a teacher and teacher educator with over 35 yea
 rs of experience in middle\, high school\, and post-secondary classrooms.
  She received her PhD in Science Education at the University of Wisconsin
 -Madison and has worked with pre- and inservice middle and high school te
 achers in schools across the U.S. Her past leadership roles include Direc
 tor of Field Experiences and Director of Teacher Education at the Univers
 ity of New Hampshire\; Senior Program Director of the Center for Classroo
 m Teaching and Learning at Education Northwest\; and Program Director of 
 the Master of Arts in Teacher Education program at the Graduate School of
  Education and Counseling at Lewis &amp\; Clark College in Portland\, OR.
  She has been trained as a Critical Friends Group Facilitator and has led
  Critical Friends Groups for teachers in all areas and grade levels\, and
  is co-editor of the newly released book\, Science Teaching for Social Ju
 stice\, published by Rethinking Schools. Liza is a certified Courage &amp
 \; Renewal facilitator who is passionate about working with teachers to c
 reate equitable and engaging learning situations for students\, and commi
 tted to supporting teachers to care for themselves in ways that allow the
 m to sustain their energy and commitment for the work of teaching.&#160\;
 Dawn Montgomery\, EdD is a change facilitator and insightful thought part
 ner. She supports leaders from a wide variety of fields\, including educa
 tors\, nonprofit executives\, and community administrators as they find t
 heir way in challenging times. Assisting humans in their discovery and re
 connection to their deepest longings has been a passion for many years. H
 er background in K-12 and college education as teacher\, principal\, and 
 district leader support her coaching practice and team facilitation. She 
 believes transformation is born when a circle of humans sit together to l
 isten\, to speak their deepest truths and to share their wildest imaginat
 ions for the world. She is expert at holding space for both individual le
 aders and teams as an executive coach\, conflict mediator\, equity-focuse
 d professional developer and a certified Courage &amp\; Renewal facilitat
 or. She is committed to making a difference in the lives of individuals a
 nd their communities.&#160\;New workshops and trainings are added to our 
 calendar regularly. For the latest on professional development related to
  your specific interests\, sign up for our mailing list! (https://lclark.
 tfaforms.net/4735441)
