 e committed to making our events accessible to all needs and abilities. W
 hen registering\, please let us know your access needs. Contact us at 503
 -768-6040 or cce@lclark.edu (mailto:cce@lclark.edu)&#160\;with questions.
 Please note: Discounted &#x2018\;Student Rate&#x2019\; registrations are 
 for current students only and do not include continuing education credit 
 (CEU/PDUs)About the InstructorJames Gurule\, MA\, LPC (https://parallelpa
 tterns.com/#)\, is a licensed professional counselor with over four decad
 es of clinical experience working in community mental health. Practicing 
 as a child and family therapist\, James also provided clinical supervisio
 n with agency staff and was designated as Lead Risk Manager at Lifeworks 
 NW.  James regularly provides professional trainings in ethics\, Solution
  Focused clinical supervision and other strength-based supervisory and cl
 inical practices. James has taught many courses for Lewis &amp\; Clark Gr
 aduate School's Center for Community Engagement\, and Lifeworks NW.New wo
 rkshops and trainings are added to our calendar regularly. For the latest
  on professional development related to your specific interests\, sign up
